  "source_text": "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nDuring review the driver describes increased thirst, frequent overnight urination and fluctuating blur over approximately three weeks, but says a diagnosis of diabetes has never been confirmed for him; his sister uses insulin, and he is concerned that this means he must have the same condition. A borrowed meter showed 16.9 mmol/L shortly after a meal, whereas another reading the next morning was 8.1 mmol/L, with no verified technique or accompanying laboratory report.\n\nHe brought an optometry card from eight months ago recording corrected right eye 6/6 and left eye 6/9, yet says the current blur varies during the day and is sometimes accompanied by glare rather than two separate images. He denies a persistent double image, has not had a current visual field examination and cannot determine whether the symptoms change when either eye is covered.\n\nThe referral mentions possible diabetes and requests further assessment, but it does not document a confirmed diagnosis, diabetic eye disease or a treatment plan. His older occupational form states vision was satisfactory at that time; the nurse has not treated that statement as proof of present visual fitness or attributed the new symptoms to a particular metabolic cause.\n",
